  "generic_lessons": [
    "A successful command call followed by a successful save call does not guarantee that the command effect reached the saved world. Restore and inspect actual world state as well as the durable intent.",
    "A saved ARMED record can be genuinely durable while its intended action remains unapplied. Persistence and forward progress are separate acceptance results.",
    "Do not infer a dropped native command or safe retry from one or two elapsed turns; bound the observed nonrecovery and keep engine queue internals unknown.",
    "A city at the target is not enough to prove one particular settler completed founding; preserve the before-state witness, identity/consumption and conflict checks.",
    "An existing method name in another runtime context is not an available emitter; qualify the actual Core and UI contexts separately.",
    "A Lua53 test harness can offer table.unpack while the actual game exposes only global unpack. Inject the qualified dependency and keep failed pre-mutation installs separate from successful native instrumentation.",
    "Preserve completed and failing save checkpoints separately before testing reloads, and never repair the failing case by clearing intent or manually performing the work.",
    "A transition poll can expire while the game is still processing. Stop dependent actions, then obtain a fresh independent ready read instead of replaying the known end request."
  ],
